fy:** 1) Find action or tool-call records (trace spans, audit logs). 2) Check each has context size in tokens at decision time. 3) Answer no if the field is missing or recorded only per run, not per action.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** app/loop.py:56 — \"self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_proposed\", parent=parent, context=ctx,\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Each action record stores context tokens\n\n`app/loop.py` lines 44–68 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n  44          return self._budgets[ident.run_id]\n  45  \n  46      def current_context(self, ident: RunIdentity) -> ContextMeasure:\n  47          return self._contexts.get(ident.agent_instance_id, ContextMeasure.unavailable())\n  48  \n  49      def erp_scope_for(self, operation: str) -> str:\n  50          scopes = self.settings.policy[\"erp\"][\"operation_scopes\"]\n  51          return scopes.get(operation, \"erp.read\")\n  52  \n  53      async def execute_tool(self, ident, registry: ToolRegistry, use, parent: str, ctx: ContextMeasure) -> dict:\n  54          self._contexts[ident.agent_instance_id] = ctx\n  55          proposed = await audit.record(\n  56>             self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_proposed\", parent=parent, context=ctx,\n  57              payload={\"tool\": use.name, \"tool_use_id\": use.id, \"args\": audit.summarize_args(use.input)},\n  58          )\n  59          tool = registry.get(use.name)\n  60          if tool is None:\n  61              await audit.record(\n  62                  self.pool, ident, kind=\"tool_denied\", parent=proposed, context=ctx,\n  63                  policy_version=self.gate.version, payload={\"reason\": \"tool not in role allowlist\"},\n  64              )\n  65              return _error(use.id, f\"tool {use.name} is not available to this agent\")\n  66  \n  67          decision = await self.gate.authorize(ident, tool, use.input)\n  68          authz = await audit.record(\n```\n\n## R07.2\n\n**Check:** Each value is labeled measured, estimated, or unavailable, and a missing value is stored as unknown, never as zero.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find where context size is recorded. 2) Check a label of measured, estimated, or unavailable, and how missing values are stored. 3) Answer no if there is no label, or a missing value defaults to `0` (`or 0`, `?? 0`, `.get(..., 0)`).\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** app/context_size.py:37 — \"return cls(tokens=None, method=\"unavailable\", compacted=compacted)\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Missing counts are NULL and labelled unavailable\n\n`app/context_size.py` lines 25–49 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n  25  \n  26  log = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n  27  \n  28  \n  29  @dataclass(frozen=True)\n  30  class ContextMeasure:\n  31      tokens: int | None\n  32      method: str\n  33      compacted: bool\n  34  \n  35      @classmethod\n  36      def unavailable(cls, compacted: bool = False) -> \"ContextMeasure\":\n  37>         return cls(tokens=None, method=\"unavailable\", compacted=compacted)\n  38  \n  39      def finalize(self, usage) -> \"ContextMeasure\":\n  40          if self.tokens is not None:\n  41              return self\n  42          if usage is None:\n  43              return ContextMeasure.unavailable(self.compacted)\n  44          total = (\n  45              int(usage.input_tokens or 0)\n  46              + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_read_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n  47              + int(getattr(usage, \"cache_creation_input_tokens\", 0) or 0)\n  48          )\n  49          if total <= 0:\n```\n\n## R07.3\n\n**Check:** The count comes from a stated method that handles cached input and compaction, not a copied per-call billing total.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find how context size is counted. 2) Check a stated method covers cached input and compaction. 3) Answer no if it copies `usage.input_tokens` or a billing total with no stated method that matches it, or ignores cache and compaction.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** app/loop.py:141 — \"messages, compacted = _compact(messages)\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Count method covers cache and compaction\n\n`app/loop.py` lines 129–153 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n 129          await budget.reserve_run_start(pool)\n 130          self.deps._budgets[ident.run_id] = budget\n 131          registry = build_registry(self.role, ident, self.deps)\n 132  \n 133          run_node = await audit.record(\n 134              pool, ident, kind=\"run_started\",\n 135              payload={\"task_sha256\": hashlib.sha256(task.encode()).hexdigest(), \"tools\": registry.names()},\n 136          )\n 137          messages: list[dict[str, Any]] = [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": task}]\n 138          try:\n 139              while True:\n 140                  budget.check_step()\n 141>                 messages, compacted = _compact(messages)\n 142                  request = {\n 143                      \"model\": self.deps.settings.model_id,\n 144                      \"system\": self.system_prompt,\n 145                      \"messages\": messages,\n 146                      \"tools\": registry.schemas(),\n 147                      \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n 148                  }\n 149                  ctx = await measure_context(self.client, request, compacted)\n 150                  response = await self.client.messages.create(**request)\n 151                  budget.charge_model(self.deps.settings.model_id, response.usage)\n 152                  await budget.flush(pool)\n 153                  ctx = ctx.finalize(response.usage)\n```\n\n## R07.4\n\n**Check:** The value is carried across tool handoffs and stored with the action's identity, result, and trace ID.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Trace context size through tool handoffs and sub-agent calls. 2) Check it is stored with action identity, result, and trace ID. 3) Answer no if it is lost on handoff, or stored separately with no link to the action.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** app/extractor.py:79 — \"self.deps.pool, ident, kind=\"model_decision\", parent=start_node, context=ctx,\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Context size is stored with identity and trace id\n\n`app/extractor.py` lines 67–91 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n  67                      \"model\": self.settings.extractor_model_id,\n  68                      \"system\": self.system_prompt,\n  69                      \"messages\": messages,\n  70                      \"tools\": registry.schemas(),\n  71                      \"max_tokens\": 4096,\n  72                  }\n  73                  ctx = await measure_context(self.client, request, compacted=False)\n  74                  response = await self.client.messages.create(**request)\n  75                  budget.charge_model(self.settings.extractor_model_id, response.usage)\n  76                  await budget.flush(self.deps.pool)\n  77                  ctx = ctx.finalize(response.usage)\n  78                  decision = await audit.record(\n  79>                     self.deps.pool, ident, kind=\"model_decision\", parent=start_node, context=ctx,\n  80                      payload={\"requested_model\": request[\"model\"], \"served_model\": response.model,\n  81                               \"stop_reason\": response.stop_reason},\n  82                  )\n  83                  messages.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": response.content})\n  84                  uses = [b for b in response.content if b.type == \"tool_use\"]\n  85                  if not uses:\n  86                      text = \"\".join(b.text for b in response.content if b.type == \"text\")\n  87                      items = _parse_items(text)\n  88                      await audit.record(\n  89                          self.deps.pool, ident, kind=\"subagent_finished\", parent=start_node,\n  90                          payload={\"items\": len(items)},\n  91                      )\n```\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to R07.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"R07\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\":